{
    "background_story": "Forest was a quiet and introspective artist who lived on the outskirts of town. His unconventional style and avant-garde approach to painting often left the local art community perplexed. While some saw his work as genius, others dismissed it as chaotic and nonsensical. Forest's unique perspective on the world was rooted in his experiences as a synesthete, where he saw numbers and sounds as vibrant colors. This blending of senses inspired his art, but also made it difficult for others to understand. Despite the mixed reactions, Forest continued to create, driven by an inner voice that only he could hear. His art was a reflection of his inner world, a world that few could comprehend, but one that he knew was authentic and true.",
